{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
  "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Alan Gura",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GURA: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Although Chicago's ordinances cannot survive the faithful application of due process doctrines, there is an even simpler, more essential reason for reversing the lower court's judgment. The Constitution's plain text, as understood by the people that ratified it, mandates this result."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What injustice has -- has been caused by it that we have to remedy? Meaning States have relied on having no grand juries; States have relied on not having civil trials in certain money cases; they have relied on regulating the use of firearms based on us, the Court, not incorporating the Privileges and Immunities Clause in the way that you identify it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Gura, do you think it\u2019s at all easier to bring the Second Amendment under the Privileges and Immunities Clause than it is to bring it under our established law of substantive due process?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Under this court's existing jurisprudence, the case for incorporating the Second Amendment through the Due Process Clause is remarkably straightforward. The Second Amendment, like the First and the Fourth, protects a fundamental preexisting right that is guaranteed to the people -- -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: When is the last time an opinion of ours made that the test, implicit in the concept of ordered liberty? It sounds very nice. But when is the last time we used it? I think it was 1937."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is the right to trial by jury implicit in the concept of ordered liberty?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What basis would there be to -- to deny that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Let me see if I understand your argument. I thought you said a minute ago that if a State or local government were to ban firearms completely, this Court might hold that that violates substantive due process because the right to use a firearm for self-defense is -- might be held to be implicit in the concept of ordered liberty; is that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Would you be happy if we incorporated it and said reasonable regulation is part of the incorporation? And how do we do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feldman",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, it's just our view would be that what Chicago has done here, which is permit you to have a -- permit you to have long guns but ban handguns, is the kind of regulation that throughout our history jurisdictions in their own -- that are most familiar with their own particular needs, their own particular problems, and in a position to balance the -- the need for self-defense with the risks to the use of firearms -- for violence, for accidental death, and for suicide -- that the City of Chicago has come up with something that is well within our tradition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: What are examples of those? The jury trial in civil cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gura",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GURA: Well, apart from the Second Amendment right, which is being denied to people in the United States by Chicago at least, there are other rights -- other rights enumerated in the first eight amendments that were thought to be the personal guarantees as well as certain unenumerated rights which were understood to be part of --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, does it include the right to contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d248debab271f27f098161db18a1e41be7a822e4a95bb4a2f9107ac539f8cc09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d248debab271-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The case is submitted."
    },
